{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["Adjacent is 'When you reap your harvest in your field' to 'You shall not pervert justice.' This teaches that you must know the laws of harvest, as in that which was taught: two are gleanings, three are not gleanings." "<b>That He may bless you</b> and adjacent to it is 'When you beat your olive trees you shall not go over them after you.' This teaches that the olive is a sign of blessing. And olive is juxtaposed to field to teach: just as one leaves pe'ah in a field, so too one must leave pe'ah in a tree."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:36.674221667Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}